## Quick start

```bash
# 1. Set up the virtualenv
python3.11 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# 2. Copy the env template + fill in real values
cp .env.example .env

# 3. Initialize the database (once created)
# ... project-specific instructions here ...

# 4. Run
python run.py
```

## Development

Tests:

```bash
pytest -q
pytest --cov=modules -q  # with coverage
```

Lint + type-check:

```bash
ruff check .
mypy modules/
```

## Process engine

This project uses [`8colors-process-engine`](https://github.com/sanishsk/8colors-process-engine).
Agents, hooks, and workflow rules are wired via `pe install`. See
`docs/process-engine/` for the reference docs, and the "8colors-
process-engine wiring" section of `CLAUDE.md`.

## Repository layout

- `modules/` — feature modules (one directory per bounded context)
- `tests/` — pytest suite (mirrors `modules/` layout)
- `scripts/` — CLI + one-shot scripts
- `migrations/` — schema migrations (numbered, in commit order)
- `docs/` — architecture + design docs + process-engine references
- `run.py` — Flask entrypoint

